{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"jaime escalante\" students future)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1039848851#14_1878661556","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2123","rank":1,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1039848851#14_1878661556\" , \"end_char\": 7136.000000 , \"headings\": \"Teacher Portrayed in 'Stand And Deliver' Dies Obituaries Teacher Portrayed in 'Stand And Deliver' Dies Students 'Stand And Deliver' For Former Teacher 'Barrio Kids' Web Resources After-Hours Tutoring Giving Back To 'Kimo' Fund public radio's <cover>future \" , \"segment\": \"AP The lawn in front of Garfield High School in East Los Angeles was sodden from the morning's rain. But the weather didn't dampen the enthusiasm of many Garfield graduates, who came from all over Los Angeles and beyond to show their support for their former teacher, Jaime Escalante. Escalante's former students </cover>recently learned he is in the end stages of bladder cancer that has spread throughout his body. The medical costs have depleted Escalante's savings, and the students are determined to help out. 'Barrio Kids' To the astonishment of the outside world, Escalante taught many of these returning graduates math — advanced math, like trigonometry and calculus. Garfield educates some of Los Angeles' poorest students, many of them from immigrant "}}
