{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_586753098#18_1198896575","relevance":3,"reason":"The Encyclopedia.com passage directly describes how Escalante encouraged students: he challenged them with tougher classes, used an unorthodox mix of discipline and encouragement, taught them to believe in themselves, told them they could succeed at everything if they had 'ganas' or desire, and decorated his classroom with inspirational sayings and posters.","learned":"Escalante helped students envision better futures by challenging them academically, teaching self-belief, emphasizing 'ganas' as the desire needed to succeed, and surrounding them with inspirational messages."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q2170","reason":"This query has produced a strong Encyclopedia.com passage about Escalante's encouragement methods; continue for more direct segments about self-belief, success, ganas, college, careers, or future achievement."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2170"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_586753098#19_1198898316","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2170","rank":4,"snippet":"He was not afraid to yell at students for being late or lazy, but he also gave them encouragement and taught them to believe in themselves. He told them that they <cover>could succeed at everything if they had the ganas, the desire. He decorated his classroom with inspirational sayings and sports posters. He was imaginative in his techniques to get his points across. He once brought a meat cleaver and an apple to class to teach his students fractions. He would wear funny hats, make jokes about sex, and do whatever he could think of to get his students' attention — and he was successful. He soon gained the students' respect and they nicknamed him Kemo Sabe, the man who knows, which was Tonto's name for the famous Lone Ranger. Garfield's students began to rise to the challenge set forth by Escalante. When he introduced calculus in 1979 he had five students in the class.\" , \"start_char\": 8521.000000 , \"title\": \"Jaime Escalante | </cover>Encyclopedia.com\" , \"url\": \"https://www.encyclopedia.com/people/social-sciences-and-law/political-science-biographies/jaime-escalante\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1039848851#14_1878661556","rank":3,"relevance":1}]}}
