{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"jaime escalante\" ganas (+ \"college\" \"careers\" \"future\" \"succeed\" \"believe in themselves\"))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_29_1127365340#16_2542333736","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2171","rank":1,"snippet":"\"headings\": \"9 Reasons Being a TA Rocks 9 Reasons Being a TA Rocks Are you ready to discover your college program? 1. Build Mad Skills 2. Become Best Buds With Your Professor 3. Win Friends and Influence Classmates 4. Take a Crash Course 5. Earn Personal Gratification 6. Play To the Crowd 7. Get a Shot at the Big Leagues 8. Get Together (Come On People Now...) 9. Attain Wisdom It Takes Ganas: Jaime Escalante's Secret to Inspired Learning It Takes <cover>Ganas: Jaime Escalante''s Secret to Inspired Learning \" , \"segment\": \"Some educators work their whole lives without ever teaching at the college </cover>level. But you are special. You get to do it while still working through your own education. This is a unique arrangement that gives you keen insight into the types of instructional methods that work and those that don't. It may or may not be your ambition to work in education, but this experience will ensure that the option is always in your back pocket. 8. Get Together (Come On People Now...) It's easy to feel a sense of isolation when you're buried under "}}
