{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"jaime escalante\" (+ \"control\" \"future\" \"futures\") (+ education math college careers))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_29_1127376148#19_2542372086","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2178","rank":3,"snippet":"Is There A Manager I Can Talk To? 4. Your Deadlines Don't Count As Much As My Real Professor's, Right? 5. You Can't Handle the Truth! 6. Dude, Leave Me Alone! 7. So Tired…So Very Tired 8. No Playing Hooky For You 9. TA Labor Laws? It Takes Ganas: Jaime Escalante's Secret to Inspired Learning It Takes Ganas: <cover>Jaime Escalante''s Secret to Inspired Learning \" , \"segment\": \"Perhaps you had the opportunity to attend an event of importance to your future career. Maybe you just hit the snooze button one too many times and before you knew it, it was time to get up for lunch. Whatever your reasons, every student gets the occasional pass here or there. It's that kind of flexibility that makes college </cover>awesome. But as a TA, you surrender some of that flexibility. If you miss your own class once in a rare while, chances are nobody will notice. If you miss your TA session, you'll have 30 college kids asking where you are and deriding you mercilessly on social media. Trust me, you don't want to become a meme. 9. TA Labor ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1595169849#1_3557777191","rank":1,"relevance":1},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1595169849#0_3557775535","rank":2,"relevance":1}]}}
