{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_13_675151580#14_1525686343","relevance":2,"reason":"The passage directly supports the idea that Escalante linked calculus to further study and each student's future, but the document is primarily about brain-based learning rather than being dedicated to Escalante or the specific information need.","learned":"One educational analysis says Escalante made calculus a way of life and source of pride, linking mathematics to further study and the individual student's future."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q2181","reason":"This query is producing relevant passages that connect Escalante's teaching to college, careers, math, and students' futures; continue to look for more direct and dedicated evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2181"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_13_675151580#13_1525684520","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2181","rank":6,"snippet":"learning to occur: “ relaxed alertness,” “orchestrated immersion,” and “active processing.” An optimal state of mind that we call relaxed alertness, consisting of low threat and high challenge. The orchestrated immersion of the learner in multiple, complex, authentic experience. The regular, active processing of experience as the basis for making meaning. (Caine and Caine 1997) Real-life Examples Rather than offering a list of “how to’s,” Caine and Caine provide many illustrations of how these three elements may manifest themselves in real-life learning situations. They analyze, for instance, the success of famous math teacher Jaime Escalante, whose <cover>students from the Los Angeles barrio passed the calculus advanced placement exam in astounding numbers. They claim that Escalante, whose teaching career was portrayed in the movie “Stand and Deliver,” </cover>was using brain-based practices: “ Although we question his textbook approach to the content of the subject, he understands his students and the world students live in.\" , \"start_char\": 7182.000000 , \"title\": \"What is \\\"Brain-Based Learning\\\"? - Brain Connection\" , \"url\": \"https://brainconnection.brainhq.com/2004/03/26/what-is-brain-based-learning/\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_345449932#1_824518445","rank":3,"relevance":1},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_345449932#0_824515965","rank":4,"relevance":1},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1039848851#7_1878652119","rank":5,"relevance":3}]}}
