{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_586753098#21_1198901672","relevance":2,"reason":"The passage is from a dedicated Jaime Escalante biography and supports his methods by noting that AP calculus could earn college credits and that Escalante recruited more students, held after-school and Saturday sessions, and tutored struggling students. However, it does not explicitly explain how he encouraged students to envision their futures beyond this academic pathway.","learned":"Escalante expanded students' college-oriented opportunities by recruiting them into AP calculus, emphasizing college-credit potential, and providing after-school, Saturday, and tutoring support."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q2187","reason":"The broad focused query is still yielding substantive Escalante biography segments with education/college support; continue to look for more direct passages about encouragement, college, careers, jobs, and future vision."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2187"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_586753098#20_1198900026","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2187","rank":9,"snippet":"and an apple to class to teach his students fractions. He would wear funny hats, make jokes about sex, and do whatever he could think of to get his students' attention — and he was successful. He soon gained the students' respect and they nicknamed him Kemo Sabe, the man who knows, which was Tonto's name for the famous Lone Ranger. Garfield's students began to rise to the challenge set forth by Escalante. When he introduced calculus in 1979 he had five students in the class. All five took the Advanced Placement (AP) exam for <cover>calculus and four of them passed. This standardized test gave passing students college credits. It was so difficult that only two percent of American high school students even attempted it. Escalante was inspired by this success and worked even harder to recruit more students. He held special after-school sessions and Saturday classes to prepare students for the AP test.\" , \"start_char\": 9010.000000 , \"title\": \"Jaime Escalante | </cover>Encyclopedia.com\" , \"url\": \"https://www.encyclopedia.com/people/social-sciences-and-law/political-science-biographies/jaime-escalante\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_135588563#3_314715755","rank":6,"relevance":2},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_135588563#4_314717466","rank":7,"relevance":2},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_2119863051#4_2281921572","rank":8,"relevance":3}]}}
