{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"jaime escalante\" students future math)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_445710199#8_943389204","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2191","rank":1,"snippet":"Best Math Movies for Middle School Students 10 Best Math Movies for Middle School Students What Are The Best Math Movies for the Classroom? 1.) A Beautiful Mind (PG-13) 2.) The Man Who Knew Infinity (PG-13) 3.) Queen of Katwe (PG) 4.) Moneyball (PG-13) 5.) Stand and Deliver (PG) 6.) The Martian (PG-13) 7.) October Sky (PG) 8.) Back to the <cover>Future (PG) 9.) Hidden Figures (PG) 10.) Donald in Mathmagic Land Read More Posts About Math Education: 5 Logical Puzzles That Will Bend Your Brain 10 Free Kindergarten Math Worksheets (PDF Downloads) 10 Free Maths Puzzles with Answers! 7 Super Fun Math Logic Puzzles for Kids! \" , \"segment\": \"Jaime Escalante is a mathematics teacher in a school in a Hispanic neighborhood. Convinced that his students </cover>have potential, he adopts unconventional teaching methods to help gang members and no-hopers pass the rigorous Advanced Placement exam in calculus. Why? Stand and Deliver is an incredibly inspiring true story that is a must-see for teachers and students alike. If you are looking to motivate students of any background and inspire them to reconsider their personal limits and potential for growth and "}}
