{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1039848851#4_1878648617","relevance":3,"reason":"The NPR passage directly answers the information need: Escalante said teachers must love their subject and their students and make students see that they have a chance and opportunity in the United States to become whatever they want; he used 'ganas'—desire and drive—as his motivational battle cry.","learned":"Escalante encouraged students to envision their futures by making them see opportunity, telling them they could become whatever they wanted, and emphasizing ganas/desire and drive."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q2193","reason":"This query is producing strong NPR passages about Escalante's ganas-based encouragement and students' future opportunities; continue for one more likely direct result within the remaining judgment budget."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2193"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1039848851#3_1878647259","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2193","rank":5,"snippet":"Teacher Portrayed in 'Stand And Deliver' Dies Students 'Stand And Deliver' For Former Teacher 'Barrio Kids' Web Resources After-Hours Tutoring Giving Back To 'Kimo' Fund public radio's <cover>future \" , \"segment\": \"CLAUDIO SANCHEZ: For 20 years, the Bolivian-born Escalante taught calculus and advanced math at Garfield High School in one of east L.A.'s most notorious barrios, a place where poor, hardened street kids were not supposed to master mathematics - certainly not algebra, trigonometry, calculus. But Escalante believed that a teacher should never, ever let a student give up. So I asked him what kept you from giving up. ESCALANTE: You have to love the subject you teach. And you have to love the kids and make them see that they have a chance, opportunity, in this country to become whatever they want to. SANCHEZ: And to make it, Escalante often said, you need ganas, Spanish for desire and drive. Ganas was Escalante's battle cry, not just in motivating his students </cover>but every time he chided apathetic administrators and jaded teachers.\" , \"start_char\": 1956.000000 , \"title\": \"Teacher Portrayed in '","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_29_1127365340#8_2542320554","rank":3,"relevance":0},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1039848851#15_1878663180","rank":4,"relevance":3}]}}
